# what this machine is made of, beyond the package that carries all of it.
#
# One line per addition, with a version of its own. The image ships this file; the update channel may
# publish a newer one at a stable address; and a machine takes what it is missing and newer at, one
# entry at a time. Nothing about one entry's version can gate another's, and none of them is gated on
# the version of the operating system that carries them.
#
# Why this exists is the most expensive fault in this project's history. Everything above travelled in
# one package with one version, so when the work after 1.0.0 was called 1.1.0 and then renamed 1.0.1, a
# machine that had installed the higher number could never be reached again: apt compares against what
# is installed, and every later fix and every new application was numerically older. What the person
# saw was that updating had simply stopped working. A version per addition means the worst a mistake can
# do is delay the one thing it is about. See ADR-0069.
#
# `preloaded` means the image already contains it, and taking it is a local act: the files are there
# and are put where they belong, with no download and no network at all. That is what "preload future
# additions into the ISO" means, and it is the state everything below is in, because the image is
# where they arrived from.
#
# The versions here are not the operating system's. Each starts at 1 and moves when that addition
# changes. Nothing compares them with each other.

feature: couchbox-shell
version: 1
preloaded: yes
description: The dashboard: the tiles, the collections, the overlay, and what starts everything else.

feature: settings
version: 1
preloaded: yes
description: Sound, network, Bluetooth, controllers, display, time, updates, storage and what this machine is.

feature: store
version: 1
preloaded: yes
description: What the catalogue offers, and installing or removing it.

feature: install
version: 1
preloaded: yes
live-only: yes
description: Erase a disk and put Couchbox OS onto it. Offered only while running from the medium.

# Offered rather than preloaded, which means it arrives as couchbox-feature-files at the version above
# rather than being already on the disk (ADR-0071). It is finished and it has been asked for, and this
# entry is the whole of what makes it arrive: nothing is built for it that was not already built, and
# nothing is sent to a machine that does not read this file.
feature: files
version: 8
preloaded: no
description: Look at what is on this machine, and what is on anything plugged into it.
